cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "azarovo-martingale: martingale choice of the monitoring interval for VM memory, with anytime-valid growth detectors"
abstract: >-
  A Python library that implements the methods of the article on the martingale
  choice of the monitoring interval of KVM virtual machine memory: the interval
  from the Azuma–Hoeffding inequality with risk delta, betting (test-martingale)
  growth detectors valid at any check moment by Ville's inequality (plain,
  CUSUM-type), the joint scheduler of Fig. 3, the estimate of the largest change
  c from logs, log analysis and a command-line tool. The core uses the standard
  library only. Additions beyond the article: a mixture of bets with no tuned
  fraction and sub-Gaussian bets.
version: 0.0.1
date-released: 2026-11-11
